    "Fresh L4 remained materially above the historical L4 baseline on Protocol Validity (93.33% vs 81.36%) and Evidence Hit Rate (71.83% vs 65.51%), consistent with the replay direction while not reproducing the exact replay values.",
    "Residual unknown Evidence IDs in fresh L4 were source-identity typos that cannot be deterministically mapped without fuzzy repair; preserving them as invalid is the intended V1 boundary.",
    "A fresh L1 sample expanded one authored range from 5 raw references to 192 resolved references. This is correct under the frozen overlap rule but exposes a scorer limitation: recall-oriented Evidence Hit does not penalize broad over-citation. That should be handled, if needed, as a separate metric/evaluation issue rather than by adding heuristics to the resolver."
